Real coefficients for the element routines in this addon.

-----------------------------------
1-7 USED by/SHARED with the stokes add-on

8   deltat: timestep

9   beta: the upwinding parameter in SUPG

10  The global scaling velocity Uglobal for U in tau parameter for SUPG;
    only needed for Uscaling=coefficients%i(31)=4

11-27 USED by/SHARED with the stokes add-on

28  theta: the parameter in the theta method for time integration

29  Compression modulus K for computing the relative change in volume J
    from the pressure p:

      J = exp[-(p-p0)/K]

    NOTE: Only applies to models that are are "compressible", i.e. dependent
          on J, such as the compressible EGP model.
    NOTE: The value of K can be set independently from the value of K in the
          compressible fluid add-on. This means, that "compressible" CEs can
          be used together with incompressible fluids. However, if the
          compressible fluid add-on is used, the two values of K should
          have the same value for physical reasons.

30  Reference pressure p0, where the relative change in volume J=1, for
    computing the relative change in volume J from the pressure p:

      J = exp[-(p-p0)/K]

    NOTE: Only applies to models that are are "compressible", i.e. dependent
          on J, such as the compressible EGP model.
    NOTE: The value of p0 can be set independently from the value of p0 in the
          compressible fluid add-on. This means, that "compressible" CEs can
          be used together with incompressible fluids. However, if the
          compressible fluid add-on is used, the two values of p0 should
          have the same value for physical reasons.


31-100 reserved for future use


Storage of material data for the viscoelastic model
---------------------------------------------------

if coefficients%i(20) > 0 then:

    The material data of the viscoelastic model is stored in the real array
    coefficients%ra starting at index coefficient%i(20) for in the following
    sequence:
    ( G_i, lambda_i, (p^j_i, j=1,np), (q^j_i, j=1,nq), (r^j_i, j=1,nr),
                     (s^j_i, j=1,ns),  i=1,nmodes )
    where
      p^j_i are the np nonlinear parameters per mode and
      q^j_i are the nq adapted lambda parameters per mode.
      r^j_i are the nr adapted lambda parameters for the h(J) factor per mode.
      s^j_i are the ns adapted lambda parameters for the g(gammap) factor per
            mode.
    Example1: a two-mode PTT model with a xsi parameter:
       G1, lambda1, eps1, xsi1, G2, lambda2, eps2, xsi2
    Example2: a two-mode Giesekus model with Saramito (2009) plasticity
       G1, lambda1, alpha1, tau_y1, K1, n1, G2, lambda2, alpha2, tau_y2, K2, n2
    Example3: a two-mode EGP model with Eyring and pressure (J) dependence
       G1, lambda1, tau_ref1, beta1, G2, lambda2, tau_ref2, beta2
    Example4: a two-mode EGP model with Eyring and plastic strain dependence
       G1, lambda1, tau_ref1, Sa1, r0_1, r1_1, r2_1, G2, lambda2, tau_ref2,
       Sa2, r0_2, r1_2, r2_2

else if coefficients%i(20) < 0 then:

    The material data of the viscoelastic model is stored in the 2D real array
    coefficients%ra2(m)%a(1:np,1:nmodes) with index m=-coefficient%i(20) and
    np the number of parameters per mode.

    Example: a two-mode EGP model with Eyring and pressure (J) dependence
       coefficients%ra2(m)%a(1,:) = [ G1, lambda1, tau_ref1, beta1 ]
       coefficients%ra2(m)%a(2,:) = [ G2, lambda2, tau_ref2, beta2 ]

